      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-05-23T14:43:00Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(nut06): add method_name to mint/melt method settings (NUT-04/05) (#672)\n\n* feat(nut06): add method_name to mint/melt method settings (NUT-04/05)\n\nNUT-04/05 add a `method_name` field to the method-unit settings the mint\nadvertises at /v1/info — a human-readable name for the method (e.g.\n\"Lightning\"). cashu-ts models both NUT-04 and NUT-05 settings with a single\n`SwapMethod` type, so one addition covers both.\n\nType it as `string | null` to match the existing `<x|null>` siblings\n(`min_amount`, `max_amount`): normalizeSwapMethods coerces an absent field to\nnull so MintInfo always returns a spec-valid response. Consumers fall back to\n`method` for display when null.\n\nPurely additive on a response type, so non-breaking.\n\n* test: expect coerced method_name in normalized mint-info\n\nnormalizeSwapMethods now coerces an absent method_name to null, so the\nisSupported(5) deep-equality expectation in the wallet init test gains\nmethod_name: null on each method-unit pair.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "378cbf4a73f4085c339352e050d531f0acd56808",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cashu-ts/git/trees/378cbf4a73f4085c339352e050d531f0acd56808"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cashubtc/cashu-ts/git/commits/28e3a208020cb1dd61512ced33e815ff61d488f1",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
